---
title: Datapack entries
pageSlug: datapack-entries
mod: structure-encyclopedia
section: config
order: 2
---

Entries are ordinary datapack JSON under `data/<namespace>/structure_encyclopedia/*.json`. The server loads them and syncs the book to clients.

`structure` must be the exact registry id. `/locate structure` will tell you. `minecraft:desert_pyramid` is fine. `yourmod:cool_dungeon` is fine. A guessed name is not.

Required: `structure`, `icon` (item id), `lore` and `description` (translation keys). Optional: `sort_order` (lower first), `mobs`, `loot_items`, `loot_tables`, `tags`.

One page per structure id. To override a shipped page, replace the same path, for example `data/structureencyclopedia/structure_encyclopedia/fortress.json`, in a datapack that loads after this mod.

Display name, if you want one: `"structureencyclopedia.name.yourmod.cool_dungeon": "Cool Dungeon"`. If you skip it, the client falls back to `structure.<namespace>.<path>`.

Write the lore like a page in a real book. Two sentences beat a bullet list of mechanics. Players already fought the place. They want to know what it was.
